   "text": "{\"sections\":[{\"section\":\"summary\",\"body\":\"Briarstone Beverage Company's operating results improved against a year earlier, and both financial covenants were met at September 30, 2026 with the compliance certificate agreeing to the bank's calculations. The most important change is on the revolving line, which is over-advanced, with availability of {{fact:cd93dc75-5983-49a9-8374-b50c46e4f979}}. A reviewer has already decided the over-advance item, and the decision recorded is that a paydown is required. The reviewer should confirm that the paydown is being tracked to completion; no other item awaits a decision.\"},{\"section\":\"performance\",\"body\":\"Trailing twelve-month revenue rose to {{fact:49e4b27b-d378-4ba0-8e9d-70e4e3ce6986}} from {{fact:a4c68944-8507-4a90-b69d-78746fd0f726}}, growth of {{fact:7258dab5-87a8-4009-a9f7-4db203f05c43}}. EBITDA increased to {{fact:3b75f19b-5f5e-49c4-abe0-1ac8ed003ff8}} from {{fact:4861ecb2-c3fa-4a24-bc07-be1e5f65dec2}}, with margin broadly steady at {{fact:62cf2d22-ec7d-4734-b880-8ec8694d142b}} against {{fact:ed9cc560-a83a-41e3-a67a-7ba5d93502e9}}. Net income rose to {{fact:30d21bcb-b68e-4132-b2b3-42bc569702c4}} from {{fact:dedff0ac-6ae6-49ff-815b-de438388600f}}. Total debt fell to {{fact:af53d458-9e76-449b-ad18-943979b27255}} from {{fact:d1487c9a-8305-4a6a-943f-728099ebdc8c}}, and debt to EBITDA improved to {{fact:e86bc093-c147-49db-97ee-6b59ca0530b1}} from {{fact:f406f9ba-23d4-49f4-b5d1-2860c19626b2}}. Interest coverage rose to {{fact:767cb10d-b685-47a8-b19c-bf2e167333a5}} from {{fact:776b6ec8-1059-478c-abce-2208445a8e52}}. Liquidity remains thin: the current ratio was {{fact:06afd68f-65ed-43c0-be84-2af80a6a4122}} against {{fact:c012fcf2-c835-48d9-9ea7-9b53c02785a4}}, cash was {{fact:88890dd3-59b5-425c-9e14-009e0c27b88f}} against {{fact:7d8f9fa6-9658-415c-9bdf-e1426d28221e}}, DSO moved to {{fact:fd7d5658-4f39-409d-b9d3-66f8763b7c65}} from {{fact:5d8a96c0-0d82-46f4-acaf-c1d4ee83afbc}}, and DPO was unchanged at {{fact:7898b87e-24b0-4580-859e-3f25f35b4960}}.\"},{\"section\":\"covenants\",\"body\":\"The Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio was calculated at {{fact:80c8d0ef-20a6-4d7f-993d-0929d4044de8}} against a minimum of {{fact:31224efd-e062-458b-9da1-cce2d7f0d753}}, a cushion of {{fact:180fd87f-fb15-4863-936e-92af0f0397f8}}. The Total Leverage Ratio was calculated at {{fact:4175c91a-3bdf-4131-880e-96370807646f}} against a maximum of {{fact:8ff17d04-1181-49d1-8d1f-2485d61537ce}}, a cushion of {{fact:d1e30ee8-90c0-480f-9a2c-b3ff072fbd92}}. Both covenants are compliant. The compliance certificate reported {{fact:78c9687b-0d97-45d8-a10e-7708f3b5c6e1}} and {{fact:60eedcbd-4b54-4b90-a8ad-d418150d7ec3}} respectively, which agree with the bank's calculations.\"},{\"section\":\"collateral\",\"body\":\"As of September 30, 2026 the borrowing base for the Revolving Line of Credit shows an over-advance, with availability of {{fact:cd93dc75-5983-49a9-8374-b50c46e4f979}}. Advances exceed what the eligible collateral supports, and the borrower has no revolver headroom for working capital. No line-level mismatches were flagged on the borrowing base. The facts held do not show whether the shortfall arose from lower collateral or higher borrowings, and a reviewer may want to establish which before the next borrowing base.\"},{\"section\":\"risks\",\"body\":\"The principal open matter is the critical over-advance work item on the revolving line. A reviewer has decided that item, and the decision recorded is that a paydown is required; the facts held do not show whether the paydown has been made. The related early warning signal, low availability, fired at medium severity, reflecting availability of {{fact:cd93dc75-5983-49a9-8374-b50c46e4f979}}. No other signals fired this period. Given the current ratio of {{fact:06afd68f-65ed-43c0-be84-2af80a6a4122}}, the borrower's capacity to fund a paydown from current resources is a point for the reviewer to assess.\"}]}",
   "type": "text"
  }
